    "title": "Mets drop fifth straight in shutout loss to Braves (highlights) - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The New York Mets were stifled by Chris Sale and the Atlanta Braves on Wednesday night, dropping their fifth straight game in a 5-0 loss at Truist Park. Paul Blackburn, making just his second start of the year while filling in for the injured Kodai Senga, was hit hard early. Ronald Acuña Jr. took him deep on the very first pitch of the game, setting the tone. A walk, single, and defensive miscues, including an unusual fielding error on catcher Luis Torrens, who touched a live ball with his mask, helped Atlanta build a quick 3-0 lead in the opening frame. To his credit, Blackburn rebounded, holding the Braves off the board for the rest of his 3.2-inning outing. But a wild pitch from reliever José Butto, one Torrens could’ve blocked, allowed another run to score. The left-hander was in command all night, holding New York to just four singles over 8.2 shutout innings, striking out nine on 116 pitches. Starling Marte had two of the Mets’ four hits, while Jeff McNeil extended his on-base streak to 20 games with a fifth-inning single. Ty Adcock allowed a solo shot to Matt Olson, the first run he’s surrendered as a Met, in an otherwise solid bullpen effort. | The Mets (45-29) will try to avoid a three-game sweep and return to the win column on Thursday night with Clay Holmes set to face Spencer Strider. The first pitch is at 7:15 p.m. Get the latest headlines delivered to your inbox each morning. Sign up for our Morning Edition to start your day . FL1 on the Go! Download the free FingerLakes1.com App for iOS (iPhone, iPad) . The post Mets drop fifth straight in shutout loss to Braves (highlights) appeared first on Fingerlakes1.com .",
